Design choices made and trade-offs
Chose Azure Container Apps for managed containers, autoscaling, revisions, and scale-to-zero.
Trade-off: less control and flexibility than Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).
Split Terraform into foundation and workload layers to limit the impact of changes.
Trade-off: slightly more complexity with state and dependencies.

Problems I ran into, and how to troubleshoot them?
Ran into image pull, Key Vault access, revision, and connectivity issues.
Used logs and deployment errors to narrow down the problem.
Checked Managed Identity, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), environment variables, networking, and pipeline configuration.

What did I learn from the project?
How to separate infrastructure deployment from application deployment.
How to use Managed Identity instead of stored Azure credentials.
How to design safer deployment and rollback workflows.
How to troubleshoot across Terraform, Azure, containers, and the application.

What would I change if this were supporting real production traffic?
Add Azure Front Door and a Web Application Firewall (WAF).
Deploy across multiple regions.
Increase staging and production isolation.
Add private networking.
Improve monitoring, alerting, and security scanning.
Use canary or blue/green deployments.
